There is a problem with the assertion at https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/3670d2532bdf51abbe0b8fea22284d7ca340ffe3/compiler/rustc_public/src/unstable/convert/stable/abi.rs#L92

If any tool using `rustc_public` calls `rustc_public::mir::mono::Instance::fn_abi()` to know "what's this function's calling-convention layout?" there is a check that says "if the function is variadic, the convention must be C," which is wrong. `extern "sysv64"` variadics are also legal Rust. The stable enum has a variant for this convention already (`CallConvention::X86_64SysV`). Here is a way to reproduce the issue below.

### Environment

- `rustc 1.100.0-nightly (6bb1652a0 2026-09-22)` (`nightly-2026-09-23`)
- `rustc-dev` component installed
- x86-64 host. On aarch64 rustc rejects `extern "sysv64"` with `E0570`, so the input does not build.

### Files

`fn_abi_ice.rs` is the driver and it asks every function in the crate under compilation for its `FnAbi`.

```rust
#![feature(rustc_private)]

extern crate rustc_driver;
extern crate rustc_interface;
extern crate rustc_middle;
extern crate rustc_public;
extern crate rustc_session;

use rustc_public::CrateDef;
use rustc_public::mir::mono::Instance;
use rustc_public::run;
use std::convert::TryInto;
use std::ops::ControlFlow;

fn ask_every_function_for_its_abi() -> ControlFlow<()> {
    for item in rustc_public::all_local_items() {
        let Ok(instance) = TryInto::<Instance>::try_into(item) else { continue };
        println!("asking for the ABI of `{}`", instance.name());
        let _ = instance.fn_abi();
    }
    ControlFlow::Continue(())
}

fn main() {
    let args: Vec<String> = std::env::args().collect();
    let _ = run!(&args, ask_every_function_for_its_abi);
}
```

`repro.rs` is the input.

```rust
#[unsafe(naked)]
pub unsafe extern "sysv64" fn defined(_: u32, _: ...) -> u32 {
    core::arch::naked_asm!("")
}

unsafe extern "sysv64" {
    pub fn declared(_: u32, _: ...) -> u32;
}
```

`control.rs` is the same two shapes with the C convention + a plain function.

```rust
pub unsafe extern "C" fn defined_c(a: u32, _: ...) -> u32 { a }

unsafe extern "C" {
    pub fn declared_c(_: u32, _: ...) -> u32;
}

pub fn plain(a: u32) -> u32 { a }
```

### Steps

```console
$ rustc +nightly-2026-09-23 fn_abi_ice.rs -o fn_abi_ice

$ LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$(rustc +nightly-2026-09-23 --print target-libdir)/../lib \
      ./fn_abi_ice repro.rs --crate-type=lib
asking for the ABI of `repro::defined`

thread 'rustc' (13085) panicked at compiler/rustc_public/src/unstable/convert/stable/abi.rs:92:9:
assertion failed: !self.c_variadic || matches!(self.conv, CanonAbi::C)
note: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace
$ echo $?
101
```

```console
$ LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$(rustc +nightly-2026-09-23 --print target-libdir)/../lib \
      ./fn_abi_ice control.rs --crate-type=lib
asking for the ABI of `control::defined_c`
asking for the ABI of `control::plain`
$ echo $?
0
```

Expected: `fn_abi()` returns, or returns an `Err`, for `repro.rs` as it does for `control.rs`.

Actual: the assertion aborts compilation. 
```
thread 'rustc' panicked at compiler/rustc_public/src/unstable/convert/stable/abi.rs:92:9:
assertion failed: !self.c_variadic || matches!(self.conv, CanonAbi::C)
```

