I tried this code:

```rust
use std::io::prelude::*;
use std::process::Command;
use std::{env, thread};

const THREADS: usize = 20;
const WRITES: usize = 100;
const WRITE_SIZE: usize = 1024 * 32;

fn main() {
    let args = env::args().collect::<Vec<_>>();
    if args.len() == 1 {
        parent();
    } else {
        child();
    }
}

fn parent() {
    let me = env::current_exe().unwrap();
    let mut cmd = Command::new(me);
    cmd.arg("run-the-test");
    let output = cmd.output().unwrap();
    assert!(output.status.success());
    assert_eq!(output.stderr.len(), 0);
    assert_eq!(output.stdout.len(), WRITES * THREADS * WRITE_SIZE);
    for byte in output.stdout.iter() {
        assert_eq!(*byte, b'a');
    }
}

fn child() {
    let threads = (0..THREADS)
        .map(|_| {
            thread::spawn(|| {
                let buf = [b'a'; WRITE_SIZE];
                for _ in 0..WRITES {
                    write_all(&buf);
                }
            })
        })
        .collect::<Vec<_>>();

    for thread in threads {
        thread.join().unwrap();
    }
}

#[cfg(unix)]
fn write_all(buf: &[u8]) {
    use std::fs::File;
    use std::mem;
    use std::os::unix::prelude::*;

    let mut file = unsafe { File::from_raw_fd(1) };
    let res = file.write_all(buf);
    mem::forget(file);
    res.unwrap();
}
```

This is essentially `tests/ui/io-checks/io-stdout-blocking-writes.rs` from rust distribution.

I expected to see this happen: process exit successfully.

Instead, this happened: process hangs.

Additional findings:
- If `cmd.stderr(Stdout::inherit())` is added, the test passes. I suspect this may suggest a problem of reading two file descriptors in parallel in the parent process.
- The hang is non-deterministic, it's less reproducible with less threads; still fairly reproducible with 2 threads, not reproducible at all with 1 thread.
- Still reproducible with even 1 write if minimal size of 8192 bytes; not reproducible with 8191 bytes write.

Truss outputs from successful and failed runs of simplified version with 2 threads and single 8k write: [success](https://gist.github.com/AMDmi3/d081ae5ad8d6ccabc8d7f1e630274d8b) [hang](https://gist.github.com/AMDmi3/82e3656426ba689241b2c828c51abb8a)

