body_text:
This issue is similar to https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/161961.

Related tracking issue: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/110011

I tried this code:

```rust
struct Thing;

trait Trait {
    #[track_caller]
    async fn method(&self);
}

impl Trait for Thing {
    async fn method(&self) {
        panic!();
    }
}

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    Thing.method().await;
}
```

This code should either produce a warning, or the panic should point to the line where `method` is called and awaited.

Instead, this code does not produce any warnings, and the panic points to the line where `panic!()` was written. Adding `#![feature(async_fn_track_caller)]` to the top doesn't change this behavior.

This is incorrect, as [the reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/1.98.0/reference/attributes/codegen.html#r-attributes.codegen.track_caller.traits) says that `#[track_caller]` on a function in a trait definition should apply to that function in all impl blocks.

Also, there should probably be an `ungated_async_fn_track_caller` FCW for this code.

### Meta

Reproducible on the playground with version `1.101.0-nightly (2026-09-26 75a75c3e0a67d3fa3d03)`

