```rust
#![feature(core_intrinsics)]
#![allow(internal_features)]

use std::num::NonZeroU32;

#[inline(never)]
fn is_zero(a: &u32) -> bool {
    unsafe {
        let a: &NonZeroU32 = std::mem::transmute(a);
        let z: &NonZeroU32 = std::mem::transmute(&0u32);
        std::intrinsics::raw_eq(a, z)
    }
}

fn main() {
    let v = std::hint::black_box(0u32);
    assert!(is_zero(&v));
}
```
This program runs without UB in Miri, though it looks deeply sus. But add `RUSTFLAGS=-Zmir-enable-passes=+InstSimplify-after-simplifycfg` (or any of the other InstSimplify runs) and it will report UB.

The problem is that the `raw_eq` intrinsic documents that validity is ignored:
https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/baff6033863e38fe5f57242ea99b7f960ce9863c/library/core/src/intrinsics/mod.rs#L2582-L2584

But InstSimplify synthesizes typed copies of each referent:
https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/baff6033863e38fe5f57242ea99b7f960ce9863c/compiler/rustc_mir_transform/src/instsimplify.rs#L321-L376 (and in this case the transmutes are lowered with assumes for the ranges of the operands, which enables LLVM to do funny optimizations).

I'm not sure where the bug is here. Possibly it's in the docs?

Found by an LLM.

