```rust
use std::mem::ManuallyDrop;
fn main() {
    let mut v = 0u8;
    let p = &raw mut v;
    let mut md = ManuallyDrop::new(unsafe { &mut *p });
    unsafe {
        ManuallyDrop::drop(&mut md);
        *p = 1;
    }
    let _keep = md;
}
```
Runs fine when run with:
```
RUSTFLAGS='-Zmir-enable-passes=+Inline' cargo +nightly miri run
```
But reports UB when run with:
```
RUSTFLAGS='-Zmir-enable-passes=+Inline,+ScalarReplacementOfAggregates' cargo +nightly miri run
```

Bisection points to https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/150446, of course. I think we were should have updated a lot of MIR optimizations to handle MaybeDangling, because they've been doing a lot more aliasing analysis than I thought.

Note that the change here with #150446 is not new UB, it's _less_. This program (with optimizations off) used to encounter UB and now it doesn't. We changed the semantics to permit some programs that were previously forbidden and MIR opts still assume those programs are forbidden.

