I've been working on a PoC to share build caches between machines. Compiling the same crate for the same target gave different `.rmeta` bytes when running on an x86_64 compared to an aarch64 host in specific cases.

Since version 1.100 (which includes #154724) this will start affecting crate hashes (since they will be computed from metadata encoding). Thus, affecting other dependent crates (their hashes will be affected as well).

