compiled for the same target with the aarch64 and the x86_64 builds of the same rustc (on an Apple-silicon Mac, the x86_64 rustc runs under Rosetta):

```sh
for h in aarch64 x86_64; do
  rustc +beta-$h-apple-darwin --crate-type lib --edition 2021 --crate-name many \
    --emit metadata -C metadata=fixed --target aarch64-apple-darwin -o $h.rmeta small.rs
  RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1 rustc +beta-$h-apple-darwin -Z ls=root $h.rmeta | grep '^hash'
done
cmp -l aarch64.rmeta x86_64.rmeta | wc -l
```

I expected to see this happen: identical `.rmeta` files and the same crate hash, since the inputs and the target are the same.

Instead, this happened: 44 bytes differ, and the crate hash differs (`7c51198e62cf8a840f2052930eabec9a` on aarch64, `6e023909af23af05c69b5b2a41958563` on x86_64)

### Version it worked on

It most recently worked on: Rust 1.99.0. The `.rmeta` bytes already differ there (28 bytes for `small.rs`), but the crate hash is the same on both hosts (.rmeta files already differ on that version).

### Version with regression

<!--
Provide the version you are using that has the regression.
-->

`rustc --version --verbose`:
```
rustc 1.100.0-beta.5 (8ea38001b 2026-10-13)
binary: rustc
commit-hash: 8ea38001b9da1d6683ac5ebbc993cac89d3a09df
commit-date: 2026-10-13
host: aarch64-apple-darwin
release: 1.100.0-beta.5
LLVM version: 23.1.3
```

<!--
Did the compiler crash? If so, please provide a backtrace.
-->

### Cause

[`associated_types_for_impl_traits_in_trait_or_impl`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/e9bbadf6824e65b3583c2dda3a0926ec76df9143/compiler/rustc_middle/src/queries.rs#L1118) returns a `DefIdMap<Vec<DefId>>` that is stored in the metadata as is ([table](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/e9bbadf6824e65b3583c2dda3a0926ec76df9143/compiler/rustc_metadata/src/rmeta/mod.rs#L519), [encoder](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/e9bbadf6824e65b3583c2dda3a0926ec76df9143/compiler/rustc_metadata/src/rmeta/encoder.rs#L1713-L1714)), so its entries are written in the map's iteration order. The keys, their hashes and the insertion order are the same on both hosts, but when a key's slot is taken, [hashbrown](https://github.com/rust-lang/hashbrown) looks for a free one 16 slots at a time on x86_64 and 8 at a time on aarch64, so a colliding entry can land in a different slot.

Using an insertion-ordered `FxIndexMap`, as [#159718](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/159718) did for `DocLinkResMap`, makes the files identical on both hosts (tested with patched builds of nightly [`e9bbadf68`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/commit/e9bbadf6824e65b3583c2dda3a0926ec76df9143)).

[`collect_return_position_impl_trait_in_trait_tys`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/e9bbadf6824e65b3583c2dda3a0926ec76df9143/compiler/rustc_metadata/src/rmeta/mod.rs#L512) is stored the same way and should probably get the same change.

### Related

- [#162202](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/162202): the same query with the parallel front end, where the `DefIndex`es of these associated types vary between runs. Here the IDs are the same on both hosts; only their order differs.
- [#113990](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/113990): crate hash depending on the host tuple.
- Earlier cases of metadata encoded in hash order that differed across hosts: [#159718](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/159718) (doc links, from [#159677](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/159677)) and [#161450](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/161450) (syntax contexts, from [#129094](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/129094)).
- [#162555](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/162555) and [#162809](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/162809) fix #162202 by making these `DefId`s deterministic. They don't change the order in which this map is written, so this issue remains: `small.rs` has no `impl Trait` at all (every entry has an empty list) and still differs between hosts. #162809 touches the same metadata files a fix here would.
- The table was added in [#143783](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/143783).

