Compiler Explorer: https://godbolt.org/z/oMfKaod8G

small.rs

```rust
use std::hint::black_box;

fn f(buf: &[u8]) -> usize {
    let mut i = 0;
    while buf[i] != 0 {
        i += 1;
    }
    let mut x = i;
    for _ in 0..20 {
        let s = i % 1000 + x % 1000 + x.min(999);
        x = x.wrapping_add(s).wrapping_add(s ^ 1);
    }
    x
}

fn main() {
    println!("{}", f(black_box(&[1, 2, 3, 0])));
}
```

### Reproduce:
Correct:
```
$ rustc small.rs && ./small

56015
```
Hang:
```
$ rustc -O small.rs

(no output; still running after 30 minutes)
```

This is generated by fuzzer.

The same happens on stable 1.99.0, beta and 1.98.0. `rustc -O -C llvm-args=-disable-lsr small.rs` finishes correctly. LLVM issue: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/232176

