This is similar to #148423, but around 10 times more ridiculous.

The following (safe) program has a ~1/8 chance of compiling in a way that leads to a double free at runtime:

`dep/src/lib.rs` (proc-macro crate)
```rust
use proc_macro::TokenStream;

#[proc_macro] // this macro is impure, and may return 0 or 1 on different invocations
pub fn random(_: TokenStream) -> TokenStream {
    let n = std::hash::BuildHasher::hash_one(
        &std::hash::BuildHasherDefault::<std::hash::DefaultHasher>::new(),
        std::time::SystemTime::now(),
    ) % 2;
    n.to_string().parse().unwrap()
}

#[proc_macro_attribute]
pub fn discard(_: TokenStream, _: TokenStream) -> TokenStream {
    Default::default()
}
```

`main.rs`
```rust
trait Distinguish<const N: usize> {
    type Marker;
}
impl Distinguish<0> for () {
    type Marker = i32;
}
impl Distinguish<1> for () {
    type Marker = Box<i32>;
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy)]
#[dep::discard]
struct Target<const N: usize>(<() as Distinguish<_>>::Marker)
where // the macro call is duplicated in each derived impl
    (): Distinguish<N, Marker = <() as Distinguish<{ dep::random!() }>>::Marker>,
    Self: Clone;

struct Target<const N: usize>(<() as Distinguish<N>>::Marker)
where
    (): Distinguish<N>;

impl Clone for Target<1> {
    fn clone(&self) -> Self {
        todo!()
    }
}

fn main() {
    [Target::<1>(Box::new(1i32))].clone();
}
```

For this to happen, the stars must align as follows:
- `random!()` expands to `0` for the derived `Clone` impl (overlapping impl otherwise)
- `random!()` expands to `0` for the derived `Copy` impl ("`Copy` cannot be implemented for this type" otherwise, due to the `Box<i32>` field)
- `random!()` expands to `1` for the `TrivialClone` impl (otherwise compiles, but no double free)

The reason is that in this case, the `TrivialClone` impl causes us to copy instances of `Target<1>` in arrays due to specialization, but `Target<1>` contains a `Box<i32>`, which is thus double freed.

To reproduce, just run `cargo miri run` (maybe with `cargo clean` in between) until you get
```
error: Undefined Behavior: memory access failed: alloc290 has been freed, so this pointer is dangling
    --> /home/max/.local/share/rustup/toolchains/nightly-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/lib/rustlib/src/rust/library/alloc/src/boxed.rs:2142:17
     |
2142 | ...   self.1.deallocate(From::from(ptr.cast()), layout);
     |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Undefined Behavior occurred here
     |
```
(outside of miri, you get `free(): double free detected in tcache 2` on linux)

cc #149752

