Live Reproducer: [playground (nightly, debug)](https://play.rust-lang.org/?version=nightly&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=fd7087cb712c1be31187fec31131e1f7)

With `#![feature(async_drop)]`, dropping a `#[repr(packed)]` struct asynchronously calls the async destructor of a field with a `Pin<&mut _>` to the field where it is, unaligned, in safe code. The synchronous drop glue moves such a field to an aligned place before dropping it. Miri reports UB.

```rust
#![feature(async_drop)]
#![allow(incomplete_features)]
use std::future::{AsyncDrop, Future};
use std::pin::{Pin, pin};
use std::task::{Context, Waker};

struct A(u32);
impl Drop for A {
    fn drop(&mut self) {}
}
impl AsyncDrop for A {
    async fn drop(self: Pin<&mut Self>) {
        let addr = &raw const *self as usize;
        println!("aligned: {}", addr % align_of::<A>() == 0);
    }
}

#[repr(packed)]
struct P(u8, A);

async fn f() {
    let _p = P(0, A(0));
}

fn main() {
    let _ = pin!(f()).poll(&mut Context::from_waker(Waker::noop()));
}
```

