### What it does

I think it may make sense to suggest `map_err` simplification here. This is especially useful because `thiserror` provides automatic `#[from]` implementation


### Advantage

- shorter, simpler code

### Drawbacks

_No response_

### Example

```rust
pub enum MyErr {
    IoErr,
}

impl From<std::io::Error> for MyErr {
    fn from(_: std::io::Error) -> Self {
        MyErr::IoErr
    }
}

fn foo(e: Result<(), std::io::Error>) -> Result<(), MyErr> {
    // useless conversion here
    e.map_err(MyErr::from)?;
    // or e.map_err(|e| MyErr::from(e))?;
    // should be replaced with `e?`
    Ok(())
}
```

