{"key": "seleniumhq/selenium#18215", "repository": "SeleniumHQ/selenium", "issue_number": 18215, "github_issue_id": "5958513980", "url": "https://github.com/SeleniumHQ/selenium/issues/18215", "title": "[js] link text TypeScript locator matches links that are not rendered", "source_files": ["D:\OSS-Mentor\data\teacher_clickhouse\inventory_20261022T172108Z\issues_discovered.json"], "historical_labels": [], "beginner_difficulty_confirmed": false, "frozen": false, "decision": "availability_passed", "reason": "current_unassigned_no_observed_claim_or_open_pr", "open_pr_references": [], "claim_signals": [], "current_labels": [], "current_signal_group": "historical_signal_only", "body": "The TypeScript link-text locator reads a link's text with `innerText`. For an element that is not rendered (for example `display:none`), `innerText` falls back to the text content. So a hidden link can match an exact or partial link-text search, and the caller can get a different element back. The Closure locator used `bot.dom.getVisibleText`, which returns an empty string for hidden elements.

This was already on trunk in `javascript/atoms/typescript/find-elements.ts` (`innerText ?? textContent`). #18175 moved it unchanged into `core/locators.ts` (`getLinkText`). Qodo raised it there: https://github.com/SeleniumHQ/selenium/pull/18175#discussion_r4326286553

