body_text:
False positives: shared-variable atomicity warnings for thread-confined `FastDateParser.StrategyParser.currentIdx`

### Environment

- SpotBugs Maven plugin: `4.10.5.0`
- Project: Apache Commons Lang, `3.21.1-SNAPSHOT`
- Java: OpenJDK `21.0.12.1` (Homebrew)
- Maven: `3.10.0`
- OS: macOS, AArch64

### Description

Steps to reproduce the behavior:
```
git clone https://garydgregory@github.com/apache/commons-lang.git
git checkout 9c86ffe30
mvn spotbugs:check -Dcommons.spotbugs.impl.version=4.10.5 -Dcommons.spotbugs.plugin.version=4.10.5.0
```

Fails with:

```java
[INFO] --- spotbugs:4.10.5.0:check (default-cli) @ commons-lang3 ---
[INFO] BugInstance size is 3
[INFO] Error size is 0
[INFO] Total bugs: 3
[ERROR] Medium: Operation on the "currentIdx" shared variable in "StrategyParser" class is not atomic [org.apache.commons.lang3.time.FastDateParser$StrategyParser] At FastDateParser.java:[line 495] AT_NONATOMIC_OPERATIONS_ON_SHARED_VARIABLE
[ERROR] Medium: Shared primitive variable "currentIdx" in one thread may not yield the value of the most recent write from another thread [org.apache.commons.lang3.time.FastDateParser$StrategyParser] At FastDateParser.java:[line 474] AT_STALE_THREAD_WRITE_OF_PRIMITIVE
[ERROR] Medium: Shared primitive variable "currentIdx" in one thread may not yield the value of the most recent write from another thread [org.apache.commons.lang3.time.FastDateParser$StrategyParser] At FastDateParser.java:[line 491] AT_STALE_THREAD_WRITE_OF_PRIMITIVE
[INFO] 
```

These appear to be false positives because each `StrategyParser` instance is confined to a single invocation of `FastDateParser.init(Calendar)`. Furthermore `StrategyParser` is a `private` class only used in one call site, so it'll never be reused elsewhere.

### Relevant code

`StrategyParser` is a private, non-static inner class. It maintains a cursor while converting a date pattern into parsing strategies:

```java
private final class StrategyParser {
    private final Calendar definingCalendar;
    private int currentIdx;

    StrategyParser(final Calendar definingCalendar) {
        this.definingCalendar =
                Objects.requireNonNull(definingCalendar, "definingCalendar");
    }

    StrategyAndWidth getNextStrategy() {
        if (currentIdx >= pattern.length()) {
            return null;
        }
        final char c = pattern.charAt(currentIdx);
        if (CharUtils.isAsciiAlpha(c)) {
            return letterPattern(c);
        }
        return literal();
    }

    private StrategyAndWidth letterPattern(final char c) {
        final int begin = currentIdx;
        while (++currentIdx < pattern.length()) {
            if (pattern.charAt(currentIdx) != c) {
                break;
            }
        }
        final int width = currentIdx - begin;
        return new StrategyAndWidth(
                getStrategy(c, width, definingCalendar), width);
    }

    private StrategyAndWidth literal() {
        boolean activeQuote = false;
        final StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        while (currentIdx < pattern.length()) {
